{{also|cut-down|cutdown}}
==English==

===Pronunciation===
* {{audio|en|en-au-cut down.ogg|a=AU}}

===Verb===
{{en-verb|cut<,,cut> down}}

# {{lb|en|intransitive|literally}}  To cut [[downward]].
# {{lb|en|transitive|literally}}  To adulterate a drug.
#: {{ux|en|We need to '''cut''' the cocaine '''down'''.}}
# {{lb|en|transitive}} To bring down by cutting.
#: {{ux|en|They want to '''cut down''' several trees to make room for the parking lot.}}
# {{lb|en|idiomatic|transitive}} To [[insult]], to [[belittle]].
# {{lb|en|idiomatic}} To [[reduce]] the [[amount]] of something.
#: {{ux|en|He wants to '''cut down''' on extra steps.}}
#: {{ux|en|Please don't put the candy jar right next to my desk. I'm trying to '''cut down''' on sugar.}}
#* {{quote-journal|en|year=1961|month=October|title=The winter timetables of British Railways: London Midland Region|journal=Trains Illustrated|page=593|text=By wholesale omission of connections and by the use of a microscopic scale of photographic reproduction which makes some of the most important tables difficult to read, the size has been '''cut down''' from last winter's 580 to 520 pages only.}}
# {{lb|en|idiomatic|dated}} To [[slay]], often in great numbers.
#: {{ux|en|I will '''cut''' you '''down''' where you stand.}}
# {{lb|en|slang|intransitive|transitive}} To shoot a gun; to shoot (someone or many people), usually to kill them.
# {{lb|en|slang|transitive|AAVE}} To challenge (someone); to prove superiority to (someone).

====Usage notes====
* In all senses, the object may appear before or after the particle. If it is a pronoun, it MUST precede the particle.

